# Timer System Usage Patterns & Best Practices

## Quick Reference for Common Scenarios

### Gaming & Interactive Applications

#### Wait for UI Elements to Appear
```rust
// Monitor specific button/UI region
set_screen_monitor(
    region: { x: 800, y: 600, width: 100, height: 50 },
    threshold: 0.15,  // 15% change threshold
    check_interval_seconds: 1,
    max_duration_seconds: 300,  // 5 minute timeout
    context: { action: "click_button", ui_element: "start_game" }
)
```

#### Monitor Health/Status Bars
```rust
// Health bar monitoring (smaller threshold for subtle changes)
set_screen_monitor(
    region: { x: 50, y: 50, width: 200, height: 20 },
    threshold: 0.05,  // Sensitive to small health changes
    check_interval_seconds: 2,
    context: { action: "use_healing_item", health_critical: true }
)
```

#### Combat Detection
```rust
// Large region monitoring for enemies/combat
set_screen_monitor(
    region: { x: 400, y: 200, width: 400, height: 400 },
    threshold: 0.2,   // Higher threshold for significant movement
    check_interval_seconds: 0.5,  // Fast response time
    max_duration_seconds: 1800,
    context: { action: "combat_response", weapon_ready: true }
)
```

### File Processing & Automation

#### Download Completion Detection
```rust
// Monitor Downloads folder for new files
set_file_monitor(
    file_path: "/Users/username/Downloads/report.pdf",
    monitor_type: "Created",
    check_interval_seconds: 3,
    max_duration_seconds: 7200,  // 2 hours max wait
    context: {
        workflow: "process_download",
        file_type: "pdf",
        next_action: "extract_data"
    }
)
```

#### Configuration File Changes
```rust
// Watch config file for external changes
set_file_monitor(
    file_path: "/app/config/settings.json",
    monitor_type: "Modified",
    check_interval_seconds: 5,
    context: { action: "reload_config", restart_services: true }
)
```

#### Log File Monitoring
```rust
// Monitor log file size changes for new entries
set_file_monitor(
    file_path: "/var/log/application.log",
    monitor_type: "SizeChanged",
    check_interval_seconds: 10,
    context: { action: "parse_new_logs", alert_on_errors: true }
)
```

### Workflow & Productivity

#### Meeting/Calendar Integration
```rust
// 15-minute meeting reminder
set_timer(
    delay_seconds: 900,
    context: {
        meeting_type: "standup",
        attendees: ["team_lead", "developers"],
        preparation_needed: true
    }
)
```

#### Focus/Break Timers
```rust
// Pomodoro technique - 25 minute work session
set_timer(
    delay_seconds: 1500,
    context: {
        activity: "focused_work",
        break_type: "short",
        session_number: 3
    }
)
```

#### Application Focus Workflows
```rust
// Trigger when user switches to specific app
set_app_monitor(
    app_name: "Slack",
    monitor_state: "BecameFocused",
    context: {
        action: "check_unread_messages",
        auto_respond: true,
        priority_keywords: ["urgent", "asap"]
    }
)
```

## Performance Optimization Patterns

### Resource-Efficient Monitoring

#### Staggered Check Intervals
```rust
// High priority: 1-2 seconds (gaming, critical alerts)
// Medium priority: 5-10 seconds (file processing)
// Low priority: 30+ seconds (background monitoring)
```

#### Regional Screen Monitoring
```rust
// Instead of full screen (1920x1080):
set_screen_monitor(region: None)  // ~2MB per check

// Use targeted regions (100x100):
set_screen_monitor(
    region: { x: 100, y: 100, width: 100, height: 100 }
)  // ~40KB per check
```

#### Maximum Duration Limits
```rust
// Always set reasonable limits to prevent resource leaks
max_duration_seconds: 1800   // 30 minutes - standard
max_duration_seconds: 3600   // 1 hour - extended tasks
max_duration_seconds: 7200   // 2 hours - maximum recommended
```

### Threshold Selection Guidelines

#### Screen Monitor Thresholds
```rust
threshold: 0.01  // Extremely sensitive (mouse cursor movement)
threshold: 0.05  // High sensitivity (text changes, small UI updates)
threshold: 0.10  // Medium sensitivity (button state changes)
threshold: 0.20  // Low sensitivity (major scene changes)
threshold: 0.50  // Very low sensitivity (complete screen changes)
```

#### Context-Specific Thresholds
```rust
// Gaming UI elements
threshold: 0.15  // Good balance for UI state changes

// Dashboard monitoring
threshold: 0.08  // Catch metric updates

// Video/animation detection
threshold: 0.30  // Avoid triggering on normal playback
```

## Error Recovery & Debugging

### Common Issue Patterns

#### Screen Monitoring Not Triggering
```rust
// Debug approach: Start with full screen, low threshold
set_screen_monitor(
    // region: None,  // Comment out region first
    threshold: 0.05,  // Lower threshold
    check_interval_seconds: 1,
    max_duration_seconds: 60,  // Short test duration
    context: { debug: true }
)
```

#### File Monitoring Issues
```rust
// Try different monitor types if one fails
monitor_type: "SizeChanged"  // Instead of "Modified"

// Verify file path is absolute
file_path: "/full/absolute/path/to/file.txt"  // Not relative

// More frequent checks for debugging
check_interval_seconds: 1  // Temporary for testing
```

### Resource Monitoring
```rust
// Check active timer count
let timers = await invoke('list_timers');
console.log(`Active timers: ${timers.active_timers.length}`);

// Cancel all timers for cleanup
for (const timer of timers.active_timers) {
    await invoke('cancel_timer', { timer_id: timer.id });
}
```

## Integration with Agent Architecture

### Context Preservation Patterns
```rust
// Gaming context
context: {
    game_state: "combat",
    player_position: { x: 100, y: 200 },
    inventory: ["sword", "potion"],
    health: 75,
    next_objective: "defeat_boss"
}

// File processing context
context: {
    workflow_step: "data_import",
    file_format: "csv",
    user_session: "session_123",
    processing_options: {
        skip_header: true,
        delimiter: ",",
        encoding: "utf-8"
    }
}

// UI automation context
context: {
    automation_step: 3,
    form_data: { name: "John", email: "john@example.com" },
    retry_count: 0,
    fallback_action: "manual_intervention"
}
```

### Multi-Timer Coordination
```rust
// Set multiple related timers
// 1. Warning timer (5 minutes before)
set_timer(delay_seconds: 300, context: { type: "warning", main_task: "backup" });

// 2. Main action timer (10 minutes)
set_timer(delay_seconds: 600, context: { type: "execute", task: "backup" });

// 3. Cleanup timer (15 minutes)
set_timer(delay_seconds: 900, context: { type: "cleanup", task: "backup" });
```

## Best Practices Summary

1. **Always set max_duration_seconds** to prevent runaway tasks
2. **Use smallest possible screen regions** for better performance
3. **Choose appropriate check intervals** based on urgency
4. **Include rich context** for proper agent state restoration
5. **Cancel timers when no longer needed** to free resources
6. **Test with debug settings** before production use
7. **Monitor system performance** with many concurrent timers
8. **Use descriptive names** for easier debugging and logs

